  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He travels Southern Border as a model righteous path Gu Master, arresting demonic path cultivators and beheading vile characters, and builds a high reputation by solving countless cases.",
      "chapters": [
        170
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is tall with a ramrod straight back, wearing Gu Master clothing and a copper mask. The mask is of a plain design with an antique feeling, and has three openings that reveal his eyes and mouth. The mask does not cover his ears, exposing greying temple hairs. His lips are pursed, the contour between them as sharp as a blade. Fang Yuan first sees him as an elderly man, then names him a middle-aged man. A square amethyst plate on his belt is carved with the character five.",
      "chapters": [
        170
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When the copper mask flies away, it reveals a square face. There is no fear on his features. Two eyes shine with the vicissitudes of time and resoluteness.",
      "chapters": [
        193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "unmasked-face",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Jia Fu leaves Gu Yue village after the Bamboo Gentleman interrogation over Jia Jin Sheng’s disappearance yields no result, he vows that on returning to the family he will employ the divine investigator Tie Xue Leng to clear the matter up.",
      "chapters": [
        57
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "hired-after-jia-jin-sheng",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_gu_yue_village",
        "gu_bamboo_gentleman_gu",
        "char_jia_jin_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He reaches Qing Mao Mountain as a copper-masked rank five Gu Master, named Southern Border’s number one investigator, and joins the wolf-tide fight long enough to drive off a lightning lycan with rank five Ironfist Grappling Gu while already injured. Gu Yue Bo states he is here due to Jia Fu’s request to investigate that murder case, and Tie Xue Leng confirms it, then places his daughter Tie Ruo Nan in charge of the investigation.",
      "chapters": [
        170
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "arrival-on-qing-mao-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "gu_ironfist_grappling_gu",
        "char_gu_yue_bo",
        "char_jia_fu",
        "char_tie_ruo_nan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Before the feast invite, he tells Gu Yue Bo she has learnt at least 80% of his abilities and will work under his guidance.",
      "chapters": [
        171
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "arrival-on-qing-mao-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later he tells her that spectating from the side is not enough, so he handed her the case and tests her next step; she answers by surveying Gu Yue village before digging into case details.",
      "chapters": [
        173
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "arrival-on-qing-mao-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After she names Fang Yuan as extremely suspicious from cultivation speed and rock-gambling luck, he answers, “Yes, continue.”",
      "chapters": [
        176
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "arrival-on-qing-mao-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "His daughter says her uncle is the current Tie clan leader. In Southern Border, Tie clan is a first class powerhouse with strong foundations.",
      "chapters": [
        182
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "arrival-on-qing-mao-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_tie_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Divine Investigator falls; her father dies. He had fought Gu Yue first head intensely, and when Tie Xue Leng was at death’s door he sent Mountain Giant Puppet Gu and Iron Fist Grappling Gu to keep Tie Ruo Nan safe.",
      "chapters": [
        202
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "end-of-the-investigation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_first_gen_gu_yue",
        "gu_giant_mountain_puppet_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
